 "text": "9/30/26, 5:12 AM\nPrerequisites\n\nAdditional business partners can only be assigned to a contract account if the corresponding contract account category allows\nthis.\n\nFeatures\n\nThe master data for a contract account is divided into a part that is the same for all business partners of the contract account\n(that is, independent of the business partner) and a part that is business-partner-specific. The business partner-specific data can\nbe controlled differently for different business partners.\n\nActivities\n\nIn Customizing for Contract Accounts Receivable and Payable under |)Basic Functions \u00bb Contract Accounts \u00bb Contract Account\nRelationships \u00bb Define Contract Account/Business Partner Relationships \u201c, you define contract account relationships.\n\nThe account relationship defines the role that a business partner plays for a contract account. You can use the account\nrelationship to differentiate between multiple business partners of a contract account.\n\nee Example\n\nFor automatic payment clearing, you specify that a payment on account is always assigned to the account holder.\n\nLogging of Changes to Contract Account\n\nUse\n\nChanges to fields of the contract account are logged. The changes can be displayed in the dialog maintenance of the contract\naccount. It also contains information about who created a contract account when, and who made the last change.\n\nKey Features\n\nIn the menu, choose the transaction Extras and then choose the desired menu entry in the following table.\n\nMenu Entry                                                                                   The system displays the following:\n\nCreation Data                                                                            Who created a contract account when and last changed it\n\nThere is a difference here between general and business-partner-\nspecific data.\n\nAccount Changes                                                                       All the changes to an account.\n\nDuring execution, the system offers a selection list of all fields that\nhave previously been changed on the account. In addition, the\nsystem displays cross-business-partner and business-partner-\nspecific details regarding the creation data of the account, and\nadditional data on business partners.\n",
